                                   Fishing
    Fishing is an art form. Not everyone can just grab a stick, some twine,
and stick some glob of something on the end of a hook... NO!

    You must buy a real fishing pole, and some real bait. Once you've found 
the proper place to fish, simply bait your hook and put it in the water. But,
it's not quite so simple. Be ready to react to the fish's actions! From there
you'll need to maneuver and work that fish, in order to get him to the shore.

    Commands:
      bait hook
      fish

    Fishing works in beach, swamp, lake, and sea terrain.

Getting started:
  1. Buy a fishing pole and bait in the profession building, 4e, n from
     Center of Town.
  2. Travel to beach, swamp, lake, or sea terrain.
  3. Use 'bait hook', then 'fish'.
  4. React to the fish as it fights the line.

    As you start reeling the fish in, be careful of your line tension! Not
too soft, not too hard! The better you get at fishing, the easier it will get
to catch fish, and the better fish you'll pull up. Your Fishing skill improves
your reaction windows, fish-attraction chances, hook and catch chances, and
the quality of the fish you land.

    Successful catches can also recover profession reagents from the fish:
fish bones, fish gills, bloody fins, and fish tails.

    Fishing materials can be used by recipe cards, guildcraft, and
profession work orders. Fishing workers can also gather fish-part reagents
for you over time.

    Enjoy! And, be careful about those fish lies. We all know the truth.
